# TypeScript & React

## Semantic naming

| Use | Avoid |
|-----|-------|
| `studentId`, `PaymentRecord` | `COD_CLI`, `facturas` |
| `guardianFirstName`, `monthlyFee` | `NOMBRE`, `CUOTA` |
| `payment-history/` | `HistorialFacturas.jsx` |

Props: `{ComponentName}Props`. Files: PascalCase components, camelCase hooks/utils.

## Atomic components

One responsibility per file. Compose in features from `core/components/`:

`Button` · `Card` · `Modal` · `ConfirmDialog` · `Toast` · `DataTable` · `EmptyState`

```tsx
// BAD: 400-line page with inline table + modal + form
// GOOD: BillingPage → PaymentRecordTable, BatchBillingWizard, useBatchPreview()
```

Extract hooks when logic is reused or exceeds ~30 lines in a component.

## Patterns

- Functional components only
- No prop drilling across features — Zustand or repositories
- No hardcoded UI strings — `t('students.addButton')`
- Domain calculations stay in `domain/`, not in JSX
